{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "GHSA-2rxc-gjrp-vjhx",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unsoundness in anstream"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When given a valid UTF8 string \"ö\\x1b😀\", the function in crates/anstream/src/adapter/strip.rs will be confused. The UTF8 bytes are \\xc3\\xb6 then \\x1b then \\xf0\\x9f\\x98\\x80.\n\nWhen looping over \"non-printable bytes\" \\x1b\\xf0 will be considered as some non-printable sequence.\n\nThis will produce a broken str from the incorrectly segmented bytes via str::from_utf8_unchecked, and that should never happen.\n\nFull credit goes to @Ralith who reviewed this code and asked @burakemir to follow up."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2rxc-gjrp-vjhx",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-2rxc-gjrp-vjhx\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: anstream\nFixed Version: 0.6.8\nLink: [GHSA-2rxc-gjrp-vjhx](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2rxc-gjrp-vjhx)\nWhen given a valid UTF8 string \"ö\\x1b😀\", the function in crates/anstream/src/adapter/strip.rs will be confused. The UTF8 bytes are \\xc3\\xb6 then \\x1b then \\xf0\\x9f\\x98\\x80.\n\nWhen looping over \"non-printable bytes\" \\x1b\\xf0 will be considered as some non-printable sequence.\n\nThis will produce a broken str from the incorrectly segmented bytes via str::from_utf8_unchecked, and that should never happen.\n\nFull credit goes to @Ralith who reviewed this code and asked @burakemir to follow up.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-2rxc-gjrp-vjhx**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|anstream|0.6.8|[GHSA-2rxc-gjrp-vjhx](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2rxc-gjrp-vjhx)|\n\nWhen given a valid UTF8 string \"ö\\x1b😀\", the function in crates/anstream/src/adapter/strip.rs will be confused. The UTF8 bytes are \\xc3\\xb6 then \\x1b then \\xf0\\x9f\\x98\\x80.\n\nWhen looping over \"non-printable bytes\" \\x1b\\xf0 will be considered as some non-printable sequence.\n\nThis will produce a broken str from the incorrectly segmented bytes via str::from_utf8_unchecked, and that should never happen.\n\nFull credit goes to @Ralith who reviewed this code and asked @burakemir to follow up."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-65807",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "An issue in sd command v1.0.0 and before allows attackers to escalate  ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An issue in sd command v1.0.0 and before allows attackers to escalate privileges to root via a crafted command."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-65807",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-65807\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: sd\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-65807](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-65807)\nAn issue in sd command v1.0.0 and before allows attackers to escalate privileges to root via a crafted command.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-65807**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|sd||[CVE-2025-65807](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-65807)|\n\nAn issue in sd command v1.0.0 and before allows attackers to escalate privileges to root via a crafted command."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.71.2"
        }
